-- title:
--   Rank of a Hopf order multiplies along a Hopf quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain with fraction field $K$ of characteristic $0$, and let $A$ and $\bar A$ be commutative Hopf algebras over $K$, each also carrying an $R$-algebra structure compatible with $R \to K \to A$ (resp. $\bar A$); assume $A$ is cocommutative. Let $S \subseteq A$ be an $R$-subalgebra such that: $S$ is finite as an $R$-module; the $K$-span of $S$ is all of $A$; for every $x \in S$ the comultiplication $\Delta(x)$ lies in the range of the $R$-algebra map determined by $s \mapsto s \otimes 1$ and $s \mapsto 1 \otimes s$ on $S$, i.e. in the $R$-subalgebra of $A \otimes_K A$ generated by $S \otimes 1$ and $1 \otimes S$; the antipode of $A$ maps $S$ into $S$; and the counit sends $S$ into the image of $R$ in $K$. Let $\pi \colon A \to \bar A$ be a surjective homomorphism of $K$-bialgebras. Write $A_1 = \mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ for the equalizer of the two $K$-algebra maps $A \to A \otimes_K \bar A$ given by $(\mathrm{id} \otimes \pi) \circ \Delta$ and $a \mapsto a \otimes 1$. Then $$\operatorname{rank}_R S = \operatorname{rank}_R\bigl(S \cap A_1\bigr)\cdot \operatorname{rank}_R \pi(S),$$ where $S \cap A_1$ is the preimage of $S$ in $A_1$ under the inclusion $A_1 \hookrightarrow A$ and $\pi(S)$ is the image $R$-subalgebra of $\bar A$.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of the rank of a Hopf order along a short exact sequence $A_1 \hookrightarrow A \twoheadrightarrow \bar A$ of finite commutative Hopf algebras over $K$, the Hopf-algebra form of the multiplicativity of orders of finite flat group schemes in an exact sequence. It feeds into the construction of integral models with prescribed points for the generic fibre of a finite flat inertia-stable group scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfOrder_finrank_eq_finrank_comap_hopfKer_mul_finrank_map.lean

